  "section_notes": "The final rules are strict on S1 reporting (24-hour regulator notice, 72-hour customer notice) and S2 testing (55 °C, 5% limit, numeric per-model results to customers before purchase but not public publication). S3 permits remote shut-off only where technically feasible for new units and gives a 6-year retrofit deadline for installed units; S4 requires built-in suppression at 36 months; S5 mandates recall above 8 incidents/100k with prompt notices. The document meets the stated red-line solution, but Northwind refused to sign, claiming public disclosure despite the text requiring only customer-facing disclosure."
